# ItemCollection
### Gets all Item Collections
GET http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections

### Gets the Item Collection with id 1

GET http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections/1

### Gets the Item Collection with id 2, when deleted it should show status 1 instead of 0

GET http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections/2

### Gets the Item Collection with id 999, should return 404 if it doesn't exist

GET http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections/999

### Adds a new Item Collection

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aa",
  "ownerId": 1
}

### Should return 400 with a message explaining minimum length of 2 required

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "ownerId": 1
}

### Updates collection name for id 2

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Changed collection name"
}

### Testing if update runs with no changes, should return 200

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections/2
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Sets collection with id 2 to archived, should not show up when getting all collections afterwards

DELETE http://localhost:5260/api/ItemCollections/2

# ItemInstance
### Creates new instance with new item

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances/new-item
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mop the floors",
  "itemCollectionId": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-08T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Creates new instance from item with id 1

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": 4,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-08T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Get iteminstance with id 1

GET http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances/1

### Get all iteminstances for item collection with id 1

GET http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances?itemCollectionId=1

### Marks instance with id 1 as done

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances/1/mark-as-done

### Clears done date for instance with id 1

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances/1/clear-done-date

### Delete iteminstance with id 2

DELETE http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances/1

# Item
### Gets all items

GET http://localhost:5260/api/Items?itemCollectionId=1

### Gets item with id 3

GET http://localhost:5260/api/Items/3

### Updates item with id 4

POST http://localhost:5260/api/Items/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Changed item name"
}

### Gets item 999, should return 404

GET http://localhost:5260/api/Items/999

### Adds a weekly rule to item 3

POST http://localhost:5260/api/Items/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequencyType": 1
}

### Frequency without frequencyType, should return 400

POST http://localhost:5260/api/Items/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequency": 2
}

### Updates an existing rule on item 3, should change type and frequency, interval stays 1

POST http://localhost:5260/api/Items/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequencyType": 2,
  "frequency": 3
}

### Instance for an item that doesn't exist, should return 404

POST http://localhost:5260/api/ItemInstances
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": 999,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-08T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Changes name on item 3 for the future, should return a NEW item with a new id and the same rule

POST http://localhost:5260/api/Items/3/update-future
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Buy oat milk"
}

### Item 3 should now have no rule, and the new item should have it

GET http://localhost:5260/api/Items?itemCollectionId=1